      "tree_id": "09d670de46c3078b174bb74bb09ee23d712b625c",
      "message": "Restore iOS export with the missing Apple authentication runtime dependency (#44)\n\n## Summary\n\nLittle Say's iOS JavaScript export fails because Apple authentication\nimports `prop-types`, but the installed dependency graph does not\nprovide it. Declare it as a mobile production dependency so clean locked\ninstallations can bundle the existing Apple authentication code.\n\nThe lockfile adds only `prop-types` 15.8.1 and its required nested\n`react-is` 16.13.1. Existing package versions, integrity hashes and\nclassifications are unchanged; no provider code changes are needed.\n\nCloses #43.\n\n## Test plan and behavior evidence\n\n| Scenario | Expected and observed | Evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Install baseline and final source independently with `npm ci`, then\nresolve the import from AppleButton and export iOS. | Baseline fails\nwith missing `prop-types`. Final resolves version 15.8.1 and its\nrequired APIs, then completes the full iOS JavaScript export. Neither\ninstallation uses copied or junctioned dependencies. | [Before/After\noutput and\nreproduction](https://github.com/MChartier/little-say/blob/59a85fcf200da63e3a470c8e7847bab347a67161/README.md#before-and-after-observable-contract)\n|\n| Export Android/web and run repository checks from the fresh final\ninstallation. | Both exports pass, along with 288 tests, type checks,\nserver build and release metadata validation. | [Native\nexports](https://github.com/MChartier/little-say/blob/59a85fcf200da63e3a470c8e7847bab347a67161/issue43-native-exports.log)\n\u00b7 [Repository\nchecks](https://github.com/MChartier/little-say/blob/59a85fcf200da63e3a470c8e7847bab347a67161/issue43-check.log)\n|\n\nThis is non-UI dependency resolution; real CLI output is the observable\nBefore/After contract.\n[Provenance](https://github.com/MChartier/little-say/blob/59a85fcf200da63e3a470c8e7847bab347a67161/provenance.json)\nbinds actual master `fabb925c`, final source `a570b52c`, independent\ninstallations, commands and bundle hashes.\n\n## Limitations\n\nJavaScript export success does not establish a signed iOS build,\nTestFlight readiness, device behavior or real Apple sign-in. Those\nchecks were not performed. No credentials, provider setup, cloud build,\nrelease or deployment is included.\n\nImplementing task: `01a11ca6-7faa-7628-8031-ac89bc018019`. Independent\nreview and CI results are recorded in the PR discussion.\n\nCo-authored-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>",
